.TH "ZYPPER-DECLARATIVE" "1" "June 2026" "zypper-declarative 0.6.6" "User Commands"
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
zypper-declarative - declarative system convergence for zypper
(Machinery subset)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]zypper declarative\f[R] \f[I]verb\f[R]
[\f[I]key\f[R]=\f[I]value\f[R] \&...]
.PP
\f[B]zypper-declarative\f[R] \f[I]verb\f[R]
[\f[I]key\f[R]=\f[I]value\f[R] \&...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\f[B]zypper-declarative\f[R] converges a SUSE system to a desired
manifest expressed in the declarable subset of the SUSE Machinery system
description: the \f[B]packages\f[R], \f[B]repositories\f[R],
\f[B]services\f[R], and \f[B]config_files\f[R] scopes.
Convergence happens inside a single snapshot transaction and records
what was applied; running it twice against an unchanged manifest and an
undrifted system makes no changes (idempotent).
The tool also reads the actual state of a system into the same data
model (\f[B]describe\f[R]), prints a dry-run plan (\f[B]diff\f[R]), and
checks drift against a reference (\f[B]verify\f[R]).
.PP
The manifest\[cq]s canonical serialisation is JSON (Machinery
\f[V]format_version\f[R] 1).
YAML is an opt-in input and output serialisation of the identical data
model, selected by an explicit \f[B]format=\f[R] option or by the file
extension (\f[V].yaml\f[R]/\f[V].yml\f[R]).
The applied record is always canonical JSON.
.SH VERBS
.TP
\f[B]apply\f[R]
Converge the system to the desired manifest inside a snapshot
transaction.
.TP
\f[B]diff\f[R]
Print what \f[B]apply\f[R] would change.
Makes no modification and opens no transaction.
.TP
\f[B]verify\f[R]
Check whether the actual state equals a reference declaration (the
applied record by default, or a manifest given with
\f[B]manifest-path=\f[R]), modulo the keep-list.
.TP
\f[B]status\f[R]
Print the current declarative state: applied manifest hash, generation,
and a one-line drift summary.
.TP
\f[B]describe\f[R]
Read the actual state of the declarable scopes and emit it in the
resolved serialisation.
.SH GLOBAL COMMANDS
.TP
\f[B]version\f[R] (alias \f[B]\[en]version\f[R])
Print the program name, version, and the embedded spec hash; exit 0.
.TP
\f[B]help\f[R] (aliases \f[B]\[en]help\f[R], \f[B]-h\f[R])
Print usage; exit 0.
.PP
A bare invocation with no verb prints usage to stdout and exits 0.
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
Options are \f[B]key=value\f[R] pairs; POSIX \f[V]--flag\f[R] style is
not used for options.
.TP
\f[B]mode=\f[R]auto|external|internal
Transaction binding (default auto).
.TP
\f[B]manifest-path=\f[R]<path>
Desired manifest (apply, diff); reference manifest for verify.
.TP
\f[B]format=\f[R]json|yaml
Serialisation for this invocation\[cq]s manifest I/O.
When omitted, the file extension decides, else
\f[B]manifest-format\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]state-path=\f[R]<path>
Captured actual state for verify and diff (offline; default reads live).
.TP
\f[B]root=\f[R]<path>
Root to describe (default \[lq]/\[rq]).
.TP
\f[B]out=\f[R]<path>
describe output file (default stdout).
.TP
\f[B]on-unreadable=\f[R]error|warn
describe: fail (default) or omit+warn on an unreadable scope source.
.TP
\f[B]scope=\f[R]etc|full
describe/verify read scope; etc (default) is /etc only, full also audits
/usr and /boot (expensive, opt-in).
.PP
Other CONFIG knobs accepted as options: \f[B]manifest-format\f[R],
\f[B]repo-lock\f[R], \f[B]content-store\f[R], \f[B]keep-list\f[R],
\f[B]signature-verification\f[R], \f[B]keyring\f[R],
\f[B]activation-policy\f[R], \f[B]applied-root\f[R].
A command-line option overrides the corresponding preset value.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\f[B]0\f[R]
Success: convergence complete or no-op, system matches declaration, or
describe produced output.
.TP
\f[B]1\f[R]
Logical failure: convergence failed and discarded; verify found drift;
manifest invalid, unsafe-YAML, or unverified; state collection failed.
.TP
\f[B]2\f[R]
Invocation error: bad arguments; unknown format value; manifest
unreadable; insufficient privilege; transaction mechanism unavailable;
output path unwritable; malformed state dump.
.SH FILES
.TP
\f[I]/usr/lib/zypper-declarative/applied.json\f[R]
The applied record of the current generation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\f[B]zypper\f[R](8), \f[B]snapper\f[R](8),
\f[B]transactional-update\f[R](8)
.SH AUTHORS
Matthias G. Eckermann.
